        "content" : "Hence it follows that A(X,e) ∼= Æ(X) by sending each m ∈ A0(X,e) to m X ∈ Æ0(X) and extending by density, thereby proving (a). Since we also have m,φ A = m X,φ Æ for all m ∈ A0(X,e) and φ ∈ Lipb(X), it follows that Æ(X)∗ ∼= Lipb(X) via the pairing  ·,· Æ, establishing (b)."
