            "font" : "SFRM1000",
            "font size" : 9.963,
            "text color" : "[0.0]",
            "content" : "Proof. Using the identiﬁcation Lipb(X) ∼= Lipb(X), we can assume without loss of generality that X is closed. If φk ⇀∗ φ weakly∗ in Lipb(X), by the Banach-Steinhaus theorem, we have"
          }, {
