            "font" : "SFRM1000",
            "font size" : 9.963,
            "text color" : "[0.0]",
            "content" : "Conversely since Lipb(X) is the dual of a separable space, the weak∗-topology is compact and metrisable on norm-bounded subsets (see e.g.[Bre11, Thm.3.16, 3.28]). Therefore φk admits a weakly∗-convergent subsequence, but since this limit is uniquely determined as φ using the uniform convergence, the entire sequence φk converges weakly∗ to φ."
          }, {
